  <page_number>72</page_number>
  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Et</catchword>
    <signature />
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Humanas elegis folicitudines,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>Et vitæ fragilis præcipites fugas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>Decantat querulo carmine clarior.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4" para="true">
      <i>Illi Musa dedit pungere acumine</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Mordaci vitium pectoribus latens,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6" para="true">
      <i>Argutisque iocis &amp; sale carpere</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7" para="true">
      <i>Corruptos hominum praua sequentium</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">
      <i>Mores, atque vagæ damna licentiæ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Et si quem placido lumine respicit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10" para="true">
      <i>Phœbus, dat Cithara nectareum decus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11" para="true">
      <i>Blandæ: qua cecinit Stesichorus grauis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">
      <i>Alcaúsque minax, &amp; Rhodopeius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Orpheus: quam facili pollice Anacreon</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14" para="true">
      <i>Pulsauit teneris fœdus amoribus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15" para="true">
      <i>Olim quam Latiis attulit auribus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">
      <i>Princeps Æolium carmen ad Italos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Deduxisse modos Flaccus amabilis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18" para="true">
      <i>Sunt qui Graiugenis carmina vocibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19" para="true">
      <i>Scribunt: ast aliy Romulidas sonis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20" para="true">
      <i>Mulcent Ausonijs: Musáque vatibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Gallis dat patria ludere tibia:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22" para="true">
      <i>Paucis illa simul dona benigniór</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23" para="true">
      <i>Mittit, si Charites tergeminæ fauent,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">
      <i>Et Phœbus Cithara si pater annuit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Sic Bezam triplices ferre suum iubet</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26" para="true">
      <i>Lauros, sic variis ornat honoribus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27" para="true">
      <i>Doctum Cecropio psallere pectine:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28" para="true">
      <i>Doctum Romuleo pangere barbito.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Faint show-through from the facing page at the right margin is not transcribed. The catchword "Et" is at the lower right. Some words in the italic verse are uncertain: "Stesichorus", "Bezam" and "Ausonijs" are read as printed.</notes>
